ProsperoSunshine: Terminate App closes the session's game, if sunshine.conf asks for it

Upstream ends the app on /cancel. On the PS5 the host never closes a game by default, because that would lose unsaved
progress. With close_game_on_quit = enabled, /cancel (Moonlight's Terminate App) closes the game the session started or found
in front, through the system as from the home screen. Only /cancel calls it: a session's end and the host's shutdown leave
the game running. The game then also stays listed as running after the stream while it is in front (serverinfo, resume), as
upstream keeps its app, so Moonlight offers Resume and Quit for it. running() itself still turns 0 when the stream ends, so the
virtual pads go as before. /serverinfo first finishes the sessions still stopping, so that right after a stream "PS5 Screen"
isn't listed as running for the moment its capture takes to close: Moonlight offered Quit for it then, which never finished.

